IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc4-part8-ch2-reduction-effect`

-- Part 8 of the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Chapter 3, regulations 115 to 119: hardship payments to a claimant whose
-- award has been reduced.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit (see uc4-seat.l4).
--
-- WHO DECIDES. "The Secretary of State is satisfied" and "approved ... by the Secretary of State" are stated BOOLEAN inputs, worded as the
-- text words them. The text says "the single claimant or each joint claimant" for some conditions and "the single claimant or either
-- joint claimant" for others. A claimant's own facts are one record; a single claim has one record and a joint claim two, and the rules
-- read "each" as every record and "either" as some record. An empty list of claimants meets neither.

§ `Chapter 3 — Hardship`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 115 — Introduction`

-- This Chapter contains provisions under section 28 of the Act for hardship payments where an award is reduced under section 26 or 27.
-- It states no rule (coverage row: inert, a pure citation).
-- src:1773 | CHAPTER 3 — HARDSHIP
-- src:1774 | 115 Introduction
-- src:1775 | This Chapter contains provisions under section 28 of the Act for the making of hardship payments where the amount of an award is reduced under section 26 or 27 of the Act.
@ref reg 115 (src:1773-1775)
`reg 115 — the Chapter is about hardship payments under section 28 of the Act` MEANS
        "This Chapter contains provisions under section 28 of the Act for the making of hardship payments where the amount of an award is reduced under section 26 or 27 of the Act."

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 116 — Conditions for hardship payments`

-- Paragraph (3): the needs referred to in paragraph (2) are (a) accommodation, (b) heating, (c) food, (d) hygiene.
-- src:1776 | 116 Conditions for hardship payments
-- src:1777 | (1) The Secretary of State must make a hardship payment to a single claimant or to joint claimants only where—
-- src:1778 | (a) the claimant in respect of whose sanctionable failure the award has been reduced under section 26 or 27 of the Act is aged 18 or over;
-- src:1779 | (b) the single claimant or each joint claimant has met any compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State under regulation 104(2)(a)(i);
-- src:1780 | (c) the single claimant or either joint claimant completes and submits an application—
-- src:1781 | (i) approved for the purpose by the Secretary of State, or in such other form as the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient, and
-- src:1782 | (ii) in such manner as the Secretary of State determines;
-- src:1783 | (d) the single claimant or either joint claimant furnishes such information or evidence as the Secretary of State may require, in such manner as the Secretary of State determines:
-- src:1784 | (e) the single claimant or each joint claimant accepts that any hardship payments that are paid are recoverable;
-- src:1785 | (f) the Secretary of State is satisfied that the single claimant or each joint claimant has complied with all the work-related requirements that they were required to comply with in the 7 days preceeding the day on which the claimant or joint claimants submitted an application in accordance with sub-paragraph (c); ...
-- src:1786 | (g) the Secretary of State is satisfied that the single claimant or each joint claimant is in hardship; and
-- src:1787 | (h) the daily reduction rate in regulation 111(1) applies for the purposes of the reduction in respect of the claimant under section 26 or 27 of the Act.
-- src:1788 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(g) a single claimant or joint claimants must be considered as being in hardship only where—
-- src:1789 | (a) they cannot meet their immediate and most basic and essential needs, specified in paragraph (3), or the immediate and most basic and essential needs of a child or qualifying young person for whom the single claimant or either of the joint claimants is responsible, only because the amount of their award has been reduced—
-- src:1790 | (i) under section 26 or 27 of the Act, by the daily reduction rate set out in regulation 111(1), or
-- src:1791 | (ii) by the daily reduction rate prescribed in regulations made under section 6B(5A), 7(2A) or 9(2A) of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001 which is equivalent to the rate referred to in paragraph (i);
-- src:1792 | (b) they have made every effort to access alternative sources of support to meet, or partially meet, such needs; and
-- src:1793 | (c) they have made every effort to cease to incur any expenditure which does not relate to such needs.
-- src:1794 | (3) The needs referred to in paragraph (2) are—
-- src:1795 | (a) accommodation;
-- src:1796 | (b) heating;
-- src:1797 | (c) food;
-- src:1798 | (d) hygiene.
@ref reg 116(3) (src:1794-1798)
DECLARE `Essential need` IS ONE OF
    accommodation
    heating
    food
    hygiene
    `a need not specified in paragraph (3)`

@ref reg 116(3) (src:1794-1798)
GIVEN need IS AN `Essential need`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 116(3) — an essential need specified in paragraph (3)` need MEANS
    CONSIDER need
    WHEN accommodation THEN TRUE
    WHEN heating THEN TRUE
    WHEN food THEN TRUE
    WHEN hygiene THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a need not specified in paragraph (3)` THEN FALSE

-- Paragraph (2): a single claimant or joint claimants are considered as being in hardship only where (a) they cannot meet their immediate
-- and most basic and essential needs, specified in paragraph (3), or those of a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is
-- responsible, only because the amount of their award has been reduced (i) under section 26 or 27 by the daily reduction rate in regulation
-- 111(1), or (ii) by the equivalent daily reduction rate prescribed under section 6B(5A), 7(2A) or 9(2A) of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001;
-- (b) they have made every effort to access alternative sources of support; and (c) they have made every effort to cease to incur any
-- expenditure that does not relate to such needs.
-- out of range: sections 6B, 7 and 9 of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001 (not among the inputs): the dates they fix are stated inputs
-- out of range: regulation 5 (piece uc1): whether a person is a qualifying young person is a stated input
-- out of range: sections 26 and 27 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): whether the failure is sanctionable under them, and under which, is a stated input
@ref reg 116(2) (src:1788-1793)
DECLARE `Facts for hardship` HAS
    `essential needs that the claimants cannot meet only because the amount of their award has been reduced`                                 IS A LIST OF `Essential need`
    `essential needs of a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible that cannot be met only because the amount of the award has been reduced`   IS A LIST OF `Essential need`
    `the reduction is by the daily reduction rate set out in regulation 111(1) under section 26 or 27 of the Act`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the reduction is by the equivalent daily reduction rate prescribed in regulations made under section 6B(5A), 7(2A) or 9(2A) of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `they have made every effort to access alternative sources of support to meet, or partially meet, such needs`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `they have made every effort to cease to incur any expenditure which does not relate to such needs`                                    IS A BOOLEAN

@ref reg 116(2) (src:1788-1793)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for hardship`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 116(2) — the claimants are in hardship` facts MEANS
    `a specified need cannot be met only because of the reduction`
    AND `the reduction is of the kind described`
    AND (facts's `they have made every effort to access alternative sources of support to meet, or partially meet, such needs`)
    AND (facts's `they have made every effort to cease to incur any expenditure which does not relate to such needs`)
    WHERE
        `a specified need cannot be met only because of the reduction` MEANS
            (any (GIVEN n YIELD `reg 116(3) — an essential need specified in paragraph (3)` n) (facts's `essential needs that the claimants cannot meet only because the amount of their award has been reduced`))
            OR (any (GIVEN n YIELD `reg 116(3) — an essential need specified in paragraph (3)` n) (facts's `essential needs of a child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible that cannot be met only because the amount of the award has been reduced`))
        `the reduction is of the kind described` MEANS
            (facts's `the reduction is by the daily reduction rate set out in regulation 111(1) under section 26 or 27 of the Act`)
            OR (facts's `the reduction is by the equivalent daily reduction rate prescribed in regulations made under section 6B(5A), 7(2A) or 9(2A) of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001`)

-- Paragraph (1): the facts of one claimant that the conditions (b) to (g) turn on.
@ref reg 116(1) (src:1777-1787)
DECLARE `Hardship conditions of one claimant` HAS
    `has met any compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State under regulation 104(2)(a)(i)`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `completes and submits an application approved for the purpose by the Secretary of State, or in such other form as the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `completes and submits the application in such manner as the Secretary of State determines`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `furnishes such information or evidence as the Secretary of State may require, in such manner as the Secretary of State determines`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `accepts that any hardship payments that are paid are recoverable`                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant has complied with all the work-related requirements that they were required to comply with in the 7 days preceding the day on which the application was submitted`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant is in hardship`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN

-- Limb (a): the claimant in respect of whose sanctionable failure the award has been reduced is aged 18 or over.
@ref reg 116(1)(a) (src:1778)
GIVEN `age of the claimant in respect of whose sanctionable failure the award has been reduced` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 116(1)(a) — the sanctioned claimant is aged 18 or over` `age of the claimant in respect of whose sanctionable failure the award has been reduced` MEANS
    `age of the claimant in respect of whose sanctionable failure the award has been reduced` AT LEAST 18

-- Limb (b): the single claimant or each joint claimant has met any compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State under 104(2)(a)(i).
@ref reg 116(1)(b) (src:1779)
GIVEN claimants IS A LIST OF `Hardship conditions of one claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 116(1)(b) — each claimant has met any compliance condition` claimants MEANS
    (NOT (null claimants))
    AND (all (GIVEN c YIELD c's `has met any compliance condition specified by the Secretary of State under regulation 104(2)(a)(i)`) claimants)

-- Limb (c): the single claimant or either joint claimant completes and submits an application (i) approved for the purpose by the Secretary of
-- State, or in such other form as the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient, and (ii) in such manner as the Secretary of State determines.
@ref reg 116(1)(c) (src:1780-1782)
GIVEN claimants IS A LIST OF `Hardship conditions of one claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 116(1)(c) — a claimant completes and submits an application` claimants MEANS
    any (GIVEN c YIELD (c's `completes and submits an application approved for the purpose by the Secretary of State, or in such other form as the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient`) AND (c's `completes and submits the application in such manner as the Secretary of State determines`)) claimants

-- Limb (d): the single claimant or either joint claimant furnishes such information or evidence as the Secretary of State may require, in such
-- manner as the Secretary of State determines. The line ends with a colon where a semicolon would be expected; the conditions are read as all
-- required (fork F-116-1).
@ref reg 116(1)(d) (src:1783)
GIVEN claimants IS A LIST OF `Hardship conditions of one claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 116(1)(d) — a claimant furnishes the information or evidence required` claimants MEANS
    any (GIVEN c YIELD c's `furnishes such information or evidence as the Secretary of State may require, in such manner as the Secretary of State determines`) claimants

-- Limb (e): the single claimant or each joint claimant accepts that any hardship payments that are paid are recoverable.
@ref reg 116(1)(e) (src:1784)
GIVEN claimants IS A LIST OF `Hardship conditions of one claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 116(1)(e) — each claimant accepts that hardship payments are recoverable` claimants MEANS
    (NOT (null claimants))
    AND (all (GIVEN c YIELD c's `accepts that any hardship payments that are paid are recoverable`) claimants)

-- Limb (f): the Secretary of State is satisfied that the single claimant or each joint claimant has complied with all the work-related
-- requirements that they were required to comply with in the 7 days preceding the day the application was submitted.
@ref reg 116(1)(f) (src:1785)
GIVEN claimants IS A LIST OF `Hardship conditions of one claimant`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 116(1)(f) — each claimant has complied with the work-related requirements in the 7 days before the application` claimants MEANS
    (NOT (null claimants))
    AND (all (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant has complied with all the work-related requirements that they were required to comply with in the 7 days preceding the day on which the application was submitted`) claimants)

-- Limb (g): the Secretary of State is satisfied that the single claimant or each joint claimant is in hardship, and paragraph (2) says when
-- they may be considered to be (a necessary condition: "only where").
@ref reg 116(1)(g) (src:1786)
GIVEN claimants IS A LIST OF `Hardship conditions of one claimant`
      `the claimants are in hardship within paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 116(1)(g) — each claimant is in hardship` claimants `the claimants are in hardship within paragraph (2)` MEANS
    (NOT (null claimants))
    AND `the claimants are in hardship within paragraph (2)`
    AND (all (GIVEN c YIELD c's `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant is in hardship`) claimants)

-- Limb (h): the daily reduction rate in regulation 111(1) applies for the purposes of the reduction in respect of the claimant, that is, the
-- rate is neither the 40% of paragraph (2) nor the nil of paragraph (3) of regulation 111.
@ref reg 116(1)(h) (src:1787)
GIVEN position IS A `Position at the end of the assessment period`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 116(1)(h) — the daily reduction rate in regulation 111(1) applies` position MEANS
    (NOT (`reg 111(2) — the daily reduction rate is 40% of the rate in paragraph (1)` position))
    AND (NOT (`reg 111(3) — the daily reduction rate is nil` position))

-- Paragraph (1): the Secretary of State must make a hardship payment to a single claimant or to joint claimants only where all of (a) to (h).
@ref reg 116(1) (src:1777)
GIVEN `limb (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (g)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `limb (h)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 116(1) — the conditions for a hardship payment are met` `limb (a)` `limb (b)` `limb (c)` `limb (d)` `limb (e)` `limb (f)` `limb (g)` `limb (h)` MEANS
    `limb (a)` AND `limb (b)` AND `limb (c)` AND `limb (d)` AND `limb (e)` AND `limb (f)` AND `limb (g)` AND `limb (h)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 117 — The period of hardship payments`

-- Paragraph (1): a hardship payment is made for a period that (a) begins with the date on which all the conditions in regulation 116(1) are met,
-- and (b) unless paragraph (2) applies, ends with the day before the normal payment date for the assessment period in which they are met.
-- Paragraph (2): if the period so calculated would be 7 days or less (both ends counted: fork F-117-1), it instead ends on the normal payment
-- date for the following assessment period or, if earlier, the last day on which the award is to be reduced under section 26 or 27 or under
-- section 6B(5A), 7(2A) or 9(2A) of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001. Paragraph (3): the normal payment date is the date on which the
-- Secretary of State would normally expect to make a regular payment of universal credit for an assessment period where payments are
-- made monthly in arrears; it is a date the caller gives.
-- src:1799 | 117 The period of hardship payments
-- src:1800 | (1) A hardship payment is to be made in respect of a period which—
-- src:1801 | (a) begins with the date on which all the conditions in regulation 116(1) are met; and
-- src:1802 | (b) unless paragraph (2) applies, ends with the day before the normal payment date for the assessment period in which those conditions are met.
-- src:1803 | (2) If the period calculated in accordance with paragraph (1) would be 7 days or less, it does not end on the date referred to in paragraph (1)(b) but instead ends on the normal payment date for the following assessment period or, if earlier, the last day on which the award is to be reduced under section 26 or 27 of the Act or under section 6B(5A), 7(2A) or 9(2A) of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001.
-- src:1804 | (3) In this regulation “the normal payment date” for an assessment period is the date on which the Secretary of State would normally expect to make a regular payment of universal credit in respect of an assessment period in a case where payments of universal credit are made monthly in arrears.
@ref reg 117 (src:1799-1804)
DECLARE `Period of a hardship payment` HAS
    `first day of the period`                                                                              IS A DATE
    `last day of the period`                                                                               IS A DATE

-- out of range: sections 6B, 7 and 9 of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001 (not among the inputs): the dates they fix are stated inputs
-- out of range: sections 26 and 27 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): whether the failure is sanctionable under them, and under which, is a stated input
@ref reg 117 (src:1799-1804)
GIVEN `date on which all the conditions in regulation 116(1) are met` IS A DATE
      `normal payment date for the assessment period in which those conditions are met` IS A DATE
      `normal payment date for the following assessment period` IS A DATE
      `last day on which the award is to be reduced under section 26 or 27 of the Act or under section 6B(5A), 7(2A) or 9(2A) of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Period of a hardship payment`
`reg 117 — the period in respect of which a hardship payment is made` `date on which all the conditions in regulation 116(1) are met` `normal payment date for the assessment period in which those conditions are met` `normal payment date for the following assessment period` `last day on which the award is to be reduced under section 26 or 27 of the Act or under section 6B(5A), 7(2A) or 9(2A) of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001` MEANS
    `Period of a hardship payment` WITH
        `first day of the period` IS `date on which all the conditions in regulation 116(1) are met`
        `last day of the period` IS `the last day`
    WHERE
        `the day before the normal payment date` MEANS `normal payment date for the assessment period in which those conditions are met` MINUS 1
        `the days in the period of paragraph (1)` MEANS (Day `the day before the normal payment date` MINUS Day `date on which all the conditions in regulation 116(1) are met`) PLUS 1
        `the last day` MEANS
            IF `the days in the period of paragraph (1)` AT MOST 7
            THEN `the earlier of the following payment date and the last day of reduction`
            ELSE `the day before the normal payment date`
        `the earlier of the following payment date and the last day of reduction` MEANS
            CONSIDER `last day on which the award is to be reduced under section 26 or 27 of the Act or under section 6B(5A), 7(2A) or 9(2A) of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `normal payment date for the following assessment period`
            WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
                IF (Day lastDay MINUS Day `normal payment date for the following assessment period`) LESS THAN 0
                THEN lastDay
                ELSE `normal payment date for the following assessment period`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 118 — The amount of hardship payments`

-- The amount for each day is 60% of ((A x 12) / 365), where A is the amount of the reduction in the award calculated under regulation 110 for the
-- assessment period before the one in which the application is submitted. The text shows the formula as "[formula: 60 % o f ( (A x 12)/(365) )]",
-- the converter's rendering of an image; it is read as 60% of (A multiplied by 12, divided by 365) (fork F-118-1). The amount is rounded to
-- the penny by regulation 6(1) (fork F-41-1).
-- src:1805 | 118 The amount of hardship payments
-- src:1806 | The amount of a hardship payment for each day in respect of which such a payment is to be made is to be determined in accordance with the formula—
-- src:1807 | [formula: 60 % o f ( (A x 12)/(365) )]
-- src:1808 | where A is equal to the amount of the reduction in the single claimant's or joint claimants' award calculated under regulation 110 for the assessment period preceding the assessment period in which an application is submitted under regulation 116(1)(c).
@ref reg 118 (src:1805-1808)
GIVEN `the amount of the reduction in the award calculated under regulation 110 for the assessment period preceding the one in which the application is submitted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 118 — the amount of a hardship payment for each day` `the amount of the reduction in the award calculated under regulation 110 for the assessment period preceding the one in which the application is submitted` MEANS
    `core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny` (0.6 TIMES ((`the amount of the reduction in the award calculated under regulation 110 for the assessment period preceding the one in which the application is submitted` TIMES 12) DIVIDED BY 365))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 119 — Recoverability of hardship payments`

-- Paragraph (1): subject to paragraphs (2) and (3), hardship payments are recoverable in accordance with section 71ZH of the Social Security
-- Administration Act 1992.
-- Paragraph (2): paragraph (1) does not apply in an assessment period in which (a) the single claimant, or each joint claimant, falls within
-- section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 90; (b) where regulation 90 applies to one of the joint claimants only, the joint claimants'
-- combined monthly earnings are equal to or exceed the amount of the individual threshold; or (c) where regulation 90 applies to neither
-- the single claimant nor either joint claimant, that claimant's or the joint claimants' combined monthly earnings are equal to or exceed the
-- amount a person of the same age as the claimant, or the youngest of the joint claimants, would be paid at the hourly rate in regulation 4
-- or 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for 16 hours a week, converted to a month by multiplying by 52 and dividing
-- by 12 (rounded to the penny by regulation 6(1): fork F-41-1).
-- out of range: regulations 4 and 4A of the National Minimum Wage Regulations (not among the inputs): the hourly rate is a stated input
-- out of range: sections 19, 20 and 22 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): which work-related group the claimant is in is a stated input
-- src:1809 | 119 Recoverability of hardship payments
-- src:1810 | (1) Subject to paragraphs (2) and (3), hardship payments are recoverable in accordance with section 71ZH of the Social Security Administration Act 1992 .
-- src:1811 | (2) Paragraph (1) does not apply in relation to any assessment period in which—
-- src:1812 | (a) the single claimant, or each joint claimant, falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 90 (claimants subject to no work-related requirements – the earnings threshold);
-- src:1813 | (b) where regulation 90 applies to one of the joint claimants only, the joint claimants’ combined monthly earnings are equal to or exceed the amount of the individual threshold; or
-- src:1814 | (c) where regulation 90 does not apply to the single claimant or to either of the joint claimants, that claimant or the joint claimants’ combined monthly earnings are equal to or exceed the amount that a person of the same age as the claimant, or the youngest of the joint claimants, would be paid at the hourly rate specified in regulation 4 or regulation 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for 16 hours per week, converted to a monthly amount by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12.
-- src:1815 | (3) Paragraph (1) ceases to apply where, since the last day on which the claimant’s or the joint claimants’ award was subject to a reduction under section 26 or 27 of the Act—
-- src:1816 | (a) the single claimant, or each joint claimant, has fallen within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 90 (claimants subject to no work-related requirements – the earnings threshold);
-- src:1817 | (b) where regulation 90 applied to one of the joint claimants only, the joint claimants’ have had combined monthly earnings that are equal to or exceed the amount of the individual threshold; or
-- src:1818 | (c) where regulation 90 did not apply to the single claimant or to either of the joint claimants, that claimant or the joint claimants’ have had combined monthly earnings that are equal to or exceed the amount that a person of the same age as the claimant, or the youngest of the joint claimants, would be paid at the hourly rate specified in regulation 4 or regulation 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for 16 hours per week, converted to a monthly amount by multiplying by 52 and dividing by 12,
-- src:1819 | for a period of, or more than one period where the total of those periods amounts to, at least 6 months.
@ref reg 119(2) (src:1811-1814)
DECLARE `Facts for the recoverability of hardship payments` HAS
    `the single claimant, or each joint claimant, falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 90`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `regulation 90 applies to one of the joint claimants only`                                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `regulation 90 applies to neither the single claimant nor either joint claimant`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the single claimant's monthly earnings, or the joint claimants' combined monthly earnings`                                             IS A NUMBER
    `the amount of the individual threshold`                                                                                                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `the hourly rate in regulation 4 or 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for a person of the same age as the claimant, or the youngest of the joint claimants`   IS A NUMBER

@ref reg 119(2) (src:1811-1814)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts for the recoverability of hardship payments`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 119(2) — the assessment period is outside the recovery of paragraph (1)` facts MEANS
    (facts's `the single claimant, or each joint claimant, falls within section 19 of the Act by virtue of regulation 90`)
    OR `limb (b)`
    OR `limb (c)`
    WHERE
        `limb (b)` MEANS
            (facts's `regulation 90 applies to one of the joint claimants only`)
            AND `earnings reach the individual threshold`
        `earnings reach the individual threshold` MEANS
            CONSIDER facts's `the amount of the individual threshold`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST threshold THEN (facts's `the single claimant's monthly earnings, or the joint claimants' combined monthly earnings`) AT LEAST threshold
        `limb (c)` MEANS
            (facts's `regulation 90 applies to neither the single claimant nor either joint claimant`)
            AND ((facts's `the single claimant's monthly earnings, or the joint claimants' combined monthly earnings`) AT LEAST (`core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny` (`reg 90 — the monthly amount paid for hours a week at an hourly rate` 16 (facts's `the hourly rate in regulation 4 or 4A(1)(a) to (c) of the National Minimum Wage Regulations for a person of the same age as the claimant, or the youngest of the joint claimants`))))

-- Paragraph (3): paragraph (1) ceases to apply where, since the last day on which the award was subject to a reduction, the claimant or claimants
-- have, for a period of (or periods totalling) at least 6 months, met (a), (b) or (c) of paragraph (2) in its past tense. Each assessment
-- period is a month and counts as one when it meets the test, and periods need not run together (fork F-119-1). The list is one record for each
-- assessment period since the last day of a reduction.
-- out of range: sections 26 and 27 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (not among the inputs): whether the failure is sanctionable under them, and under which, is a stated input
@ref reg 119(3) (src:1815-1819)
GIVEN `the facts for each assessment period since the last day on which the award was subject to a reduction under section 26 or 27 of the Act` IS A LIST OF `Facts for the recoverability of hardship payments`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 119(3) — paragraph (1) has ceased to apply` `the facts for each assessment period since the last day on which the award was subject to a reduction under section 26 or 27 of the Act` MEANS
    (count (filter (GIVEN p YIELD `reg 119(2) — the assessment period is outside the recovery of paragraph (1)` p) `the facts for each assessment period since the last day on which the award was subject to a reduction under section 26 or 27 of the Act`)) AT LEAST 6

-- Paragraph (1): hardship payments are recoverable, unless paragraph (2) applies to the assessment period or paragraph (3) has ended it.
@ref reg 119(1) (src:1809-1810)
GIVEN `paragraph (2) applies to the assessment period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (3) has ceased the application of paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 119(1) — hardship payments are recoverable` `paragraph (2) applies to the assessment period` `paragraph (3) has ceased the application of paragraph (1)` MEANS
    (NOT `paragraph (2) applies to the assessment period`)
    AND (NOT `paragraph (3) has ceased the application of paragraph (1)`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The signature line`

-- The Regulations end with the line that records they were signed by authority of the Secretary of State (coverage row: inert, machinery).
-- src:1820 | Signed by authority of the Secretary of State for Work and Pensions.
@ref signature line (src:1820)
`the signature line — signed by authority of the Secretary of State for Work and Pensions` MEANS
        "Signed by authority of the Secretary of State for Work and Pensions."
